{{!
    @template local_unifiedgrader/help_section_bbb

    Help page partial: marking a BigBlueButton activity. The grader's help
    button links to #integration-bigbluebuttonbn, so that id must stay.

    Context variables:
    * img - object - Screenshot URLs keyed by file name in pix/help.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "img": {
            "bbb": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/bbb",
            "bbb_activity_points": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/bbb_activity_points"
        }
    }
}}
<section id="integration-bigbluebuttonbn" class="local-unifiedgrader-help-activity">
<h4 class="local-unifiedgrader-help-activity-title"><i class="fa fa-video-camera" aria-hidden="true"></i> BigBlueButton</h4>

<p>Grade participation in live sessions: watch the recording, see how active the student was, and
leave comments at exact moments of the recording.</p>

<h5>Choose a session</h5>
<ul>
    <li>Pills above the preview list the sessions: <strong>All sessions</strong>, then one per recording, labelled with its date.</li>
    <li>Click a pill to load that recording and to show that session's figures only.</li>
    <li><strong>Fullscreen</strong> enlarges the player. <strong>Open in new tab</strong> opens the recording on its own, which helps when the embedded player stays blank.</li>
    <li>A grey line under the pills explains when the grader cannot tell which sessions the student attended, and so shows them all.</li>
</ul>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.bbb}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.bbb}}" width="1600" height="909" loading="lazy"
             alt="A BigBlueButton activity in the grader. Session pills (All sessions and five dates) sit above Fullscreen and Open in new tab buttons and a recording player. On the right are a Mark as graded switch and the feedback editor.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>Session pills, <strong>Fullscreen</strong>, <strong>Open in new tab</strong> and the recording.
    This activity has no grade, so the panel offers <strong>Mark as graded</strong>.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h5>Comment on a moment of the recording</h5>
<p>Under the player is the <strong>Recording annotations</strong> panel.</p>
<ol>
    <li>Play to the moment you want. The <strong>Timestamp</strong> box follows the player; the clock button copies the current time.</li>
    <li>Choose a <strong>Category</strong>: General, Praise, Correction, Suggestion or Question.</li>
    <li>Write the comment, or use <strong>Insert from library</strong>. <strong>Save to library</strong> keeps it for next time.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Add comment</strong>. It joins <em>Existing comments</em>, and the student sees it with the recording.</li>
</ol>

<h5>Activity Points</h5>
<p>The <strong>Activity Points</strong> card shows six figures for the student: <strong>Chats</strong>,
<strong>Talks</strong>, <strong>Hand raises</strong>, <strong>Poll votes</strong>,
<strong>Emoji reactions</strong> and <strong>Attendance</strong> (time present). With
<em>All sessions</em> selected they are totals; with one session selected they are for that session.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Refresh attendance</strong> reads each recording's attendance again from the
        BigBlueButton server. Use it after a new recording appears, or when a student who attended shows as absent.</li>
    <li><strong>View full analytics</strong> opens BigBlueButton's own statistics for the session in a new tab.</li>
    <li>A student with no attendance shows <em>Did not attend</em>. You can still grade them.</li>
</ul>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.bbb_activity_points}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.bbb_activity_points}}" width="1600" height="909" loading="lazy"
             alt="The lower part of the BigBlueButton preview: the Recording annotations form with Timestamp, Category, a comment editor and Add comment, Insert from library and Save to library buttons; below it the Activity Points card with six tiles, Refresh attendance and View full analytics.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The <strong>Recording annotations</strong> form and the <strong>Activity Points</strong> tiles.</figcaption>
</figure>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note">
    <p><strong>If the figures are missing.</strong> The card says so and gives the reason. When the
    site is not set to receive session summaries, it offers a
    <em>Pull engagement data from BBB recordings</em> button that reads them from the recordings
    instead. Some BigBlueButton servers also supply a 0 to 10 <em>Activity Score</em>; when they do,
    it is shown above the tiles. Administrators: see
    <a href="#plugin-advgrd">BigBlueButton setup</a>.</p>
</div>

<h5>Grade</h5>
<p>Give a grade and feedback as for any activity. If your site has the BigBlueButton advanced
grading extension, a <a href="#feature-rubrics">rubric or marking guide</a> set on the activity
appears in the marking panel. BigBlueButton activities have no due date, so there are no late
penalties, extensions or status menu.</p>

<h5>Groups</h5>
<p>In a separate-groups activity, students see the recordings of their own group. A student always
sees the recording their feedback is on, even when it belongs to another group.</p>
</section>
